om chronic constipation?", "summary": "Long-standing constipation increases risk of fecal impaction or megacolon complications."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the wife's cruise-related gastrointestinal symptoms provide direct evidence for infectious enteritis in this patient?", "summary": "Household exposure to cruise-related gastroenteritis raises possibility of norovirus transmission."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the weak lower extremity pulses and systolic murmur inconsistent with a primary mechanical bowel obstruction diagnosis?", "summary": "Vascular findings don't directly contradict mechanical obstruction but suggest alternative cardiovascular considerations."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the recent acute exacerbation of symptoms and response to fatty meals inconsistent with a purely chronic constipation complication?", "summary": "Acute worsening with dietary triggers suggests a more dynamic process than typical chronic constipation."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the absence of acute ischemic features (peritonitis, severe pain) and presence of systolic murmur inconsistent with vascular insufficiency as the cause?", "summary": "Lack of ischemic signs reduces support for vascular causes despite cardiovascular findings."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the absence of fever, leukocytosis, and bloody diarrhea inconsistent with infectious enteritis as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Classic infectious features are absent, making this less likely despite potential exposure."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.331], ["B2", 0.298], ["B1.1", 0.207]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers or time-critical syndromes identified.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "No branch meets co